/*!
@defgroup sent
@ingroup mod_communication Single Edge Nibble Transmission Receiver (SENT)
@brief SAE J2716 SENT receiver peripheral driver for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The SENT module provides a hardware-based receiver for the SAE J2716 Single
Edge Nibble Transmission protocol. SENT is a point-to-point, unidirectional
communication scheme commonly used for transmitting sensor data (e.g.,
pressure, position, temperature) in automotive applications. The driver
supports multi-channel reception with configurable diagnostics, DMA offload,
and callback-driven event notification.

@section sent_features Key Features
- Reception of **Fast** (data) and **Slow** (serial) SENT messages per SAE J2716.
- Three operating modes: **Polled**, **Interrupt**, and **DMA**.
- Configurable number of data nibbles per Fast message (1–6).
- Standard and Extended Slow serial message decoding (Short 4-bit ID,
  Enhanced 4-bit ID, Enhanced 8-bit ID).
- Configurable tick duration (channel prescaler derived from peripheral clock).
- CRC verification for both Fast and Slow messages, with legacy/recommended
  CRC type selection.
- Comprehensive diagnostics: bus idle detection, calibration pulse monitoring,
  nibble value errors, CRC errors, and edge count errors.
- Pause pulse detection with configurable diagnostics.
- Successive calibration check with low-latency or preferred method.
- Hardware input filter (glitch filter) on supported devices.
- Receive polarity selection (negative/positive edge) on supported devices.
- SPC (Short PWM Code) pulse generation with software/hardware trigger on
  supported devices.
- FIFO mode for Fast message DMA transfers on supported devices.

@section sent_modes Operating Modes

The operating mode is determined by the configuration passed to SENT_DRV_Init()
and can be changed at runtime via SENT_DRV_SetRxCallbackFunction().

| Mode      | Condition                                              | Data Retrieval Method                              |
|-----------|--------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| Polled    | No callback function, DMA disabled                     | Poll SENT_DRV_GetFastRxStatus() / SENT_DRV_GetSlowRxStatus(), then read messages |
| Interrupt | Callback function provided, DMA disabled               | Read messages inside callback on SENT_CALLBACK_FAST_RX_COMPLETE / SENT_CALLBACK_SLOW_RX_COMPLETE |
| DMA       | DMA flags enabled in channel config                    | Data transferred to user buffer automatically; callback notified with SENT_CALLBACK_FAST_DMA_RX_COMPLETE / SENT_CALLBACK_SLOW_DMA_RX_COMPLETE |

@section sent_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection sent_config_channel sent_channel_config_t Fields
| Field           | Type                              | Description                                              |
|-----------------|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| channelId       | uint8_t                           | Hardware channel number (0..SENT_CH_COUNT-1).            |
| tickDuration    | uint8_t                           | Tick duration in microseconds (prescaler derived).       |
| recvPol         | sent_channel_recv_polarity_t      | Receive edge polarity (negative/positive). Feature-gated.|
| inputFilter     | sent_channel_input_filter_t       | Glitch filter width in protocol clocks. Feature-gated.   |
| diagConfig      | sent_diag_config_t                | Diagnostics configuration sub-structure.                 |
| fastMsgConfig   | sent_fast_msg_config_t            | Fast message channel configuration.                      |
| slowMsgConfig   | sent_slow_msg_config_t            | Slow message channel configuration.                      |
| spcConfig       | sent_spc_config_t                 | SPC pulse configuration. Feature-gated.                  |

@subsection sent_config_driver sent_driver_user_config_t Fields
| Field             | Type                          | Description                                            |
|-------------------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| fastMsgDmaPtr     | sent_raw_msg_t *              | DMA target buffer pointer for Fast messages.           |
| slowMsgDmaPtr     | sent_raw_msg_t *              | DMA target buffer pointer for Slow messages.           |
| callbackFunc      | sent_callback_t               | Callback function and user parameter for notifications.|
| slowDmaChannel    | uint8_t                       | DMA channel number for Slow message transfers.         |
| fastDmaChannel    | uint8_t                       | DMA channel number for Fast message transfers.         |
| fastDmaFIFOEnable | bool                          | Enable FIFO mode for Fast DMA transfers.               |
| fastDmaFIFOSize   | uint8_t                       | FIFO watermark (minimum messages before DMA trigger).  |
| channelConfig     | const sent_channel_config_t * | Pointer to array of channel configurations.            |
| numOfConfigs      | uint8_t                       | Number of entries in channelConfig array.               |

@subsection sent_config_events Diagnostic Event Masks
| Macro                  | Description                                                            |
|------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_EV_BUS_IDLE       | Channel idle longer than allowed.                                      |
| SENT_EV_SPC_END        | SPC end event occurred.                                                |
| SENT_EV_CAL_RESYNC     | Successive calibration check failed three times.                       |
| SENT_EV_CAL_20_25      | Calibration pulse variation 20–25% from 56 ticks.                      |
| SENT_EV_SMSG_OFLW      | Slow message overflow.                                                 |
| SENT_EV_FMSG_OFLW      | Fast message overflow.                                                 |
| SENT_EV_PP_DIAG_ERR    | Pause pulse ratio exceeds 1.5625% between messages.                    |
| SENT_EV_CAL_LEN_ERR    | Calibration pulse exceeds 56 ticks ± 25%.                              |
| SENT_EV_CAL_DIAG_ERR   | Successive calibration pulses differ by > 1.56%.                       |
| SENT_EV_NIB_VAL_ERR    | Nibble data value out of range (< 0 or > 15).                          |
| SENT_EV_SMSG_CRC_ERR   | Slow serial message CRC error.                                        |
| SENT_EV_FMSG_CRC_ERR   | Fast serial message CRC error.                                        |
| SENT_EV_NUM_EDGES_ERR  | Unexpected number of negative edges between calibration pulses.        |
| SENT_EV_FIFO_OVERFLOW  | FIFO queue overflow.                                                   |
| SENT_EV_FDMA_UNDERFLOW | Fast message DMA register underflow.                                   |
| SENT_EV_SDMA_UNDERFLOW | Slow message DMA register underflow.                                   |

@section sent_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection sent_usage_polled Pattern 1: Polled Mode Reception
Poll for available messages and read them when ready.

@code{.c}
#define INST_SENT (0U)

sent_state_t sentState;
sent_fast_msg_t fastMessage;
sent_slow_msg_t slowMessage;

/* Step 1: Prepare configuration (no callback = polled mode) */
sent_channel_config_t chCfg;
sent_driver_user_config_t driverCfg;
driverCfg.channelConfig = &chCfg;
SENT_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&driverCfg);

/* Step 2: Initialize */
SENT_DRV_Init(INST_SENT, &driverCfg, &sentState);

/* Step 3: Poll and read */
while (1)
{
    if (SENT_DRV_GetFastRxStatus(INST_SENT, 0U))
    {
        SENT_DRV_GetFastMsg(INST_SENT, 0U, &fastMessage);
        /* Process fastMessage.data, fastMessage.statusField, etc. */
    }

    if (SENT_DRV_GetSlowRxStatus(INST_SENT, 0U))
    {
        SENT_DRV_GetSlowMsg(INST_SENT, 0U, &slowMessage);
        /* Process slowMessage.data, slowMessage.id, slowMessage.type, etc. */
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection sent_usage_interrupt Pattern 2: Interrupt Mode Reception
Provide a callback function to be notified of incoming messages.

@code{.c}
#define INST_SENT (0U)

sent_state_t sentState;
sent_fast_msg_t fastMessage;
sent_slow_msg_t slowMessage;
sent_event_t activeEvents;

void sentCallback(uint32_t instance, uint32_t channel,
                  sent_callback_type_t type, void * param)
{
    (void)param;
    switch (type)
    {
    case SENT_CALLBACK_FAST_RX_COMPLETE:
        SENT_DRV_GetFastMsg(instance, channel, &fastMessage);
        break;

    case SENT_CALLBACK_SLOW_RX_COMPLETE:
        SENT_DRV_GetSlowMsg(instance, channel, &slowMessage);
        break;

    case SENT_CALLBACK_RX_ERROR:
        SENT_DRV_GetEvents(instance, channel, &activeEvents);
        break;

    default:
        break;
    }
}

int main(void)
{
    sent_channel_config_t chCfg;
    sent_driver_user_config_t driverCfg;
    driverCfg.channelConfig = &chCfg;
    SENT_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&driverCfg);

    /* Set callback for interrupt mode */
    driverCfg.callbackFunc.function = sentCallback;
    driverCfg.callbackFunc.param = NULL;

    SENT_DRV_Init(INST_SENT, &driverCfg, &sentState);
    INT_SYS_EnableIRQGlobal();

    while (1)
    {
        /* Messages are received asynchronously via callback */
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection sent_usage_dma Pattern 3: DMA Mode Reception
Enable DMA for automatic data transfer to user buffers.

@code{.c}
#define INST_SENT (0U)

sent_state_t sentState;
sent_raw_msg_t fastDmaBuffer[32];
sent_raw_msg_t slowDmaBuffer;
sent_fast_msg_t fastMessage;

void sentDmaCallback(uint32_t instance, uint32_t channel,
                     sent_callback_type_t type, void * param)
{
    (void)param;
    if (type == SENT_CALLBACK_FAST_DMA_RX_COMPLETE)
    {
        /* Convert raw DMA data to structured message */
        SENT_DRV_GetFastMsgFromRaw(&fastMessage, &fastDmaBuffer[0]);
    }
}

int main(void)
{
    sent_channel_config_t chCfg;
    sent_driver_user_config_t driverCfg;
    driverCfg.channelConfig = &chCfg;
    SENT_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&driverCfg);

    /* Enable DMA */
    chCfg.fastMsgConfig.dmaEnable = true;
    driverCfg.fastMsgDmaPtr = fastDmaBuffer;
    driverCfg.slowMsgDmaPtr = &slowDmaBuffer;
    driverCfg.fastDmaChannel = 0U;
    driverCfg.slowDmaChannel = 1U;
    driverCfg.callbackFunc.function = sentDmaCallback;
    driverCfg.callbackFunc.param = NULL;

    SENT_DRV_Init(INST_SENT, &driverCfg, &sentState);
    INT_SYS_EnableIRQGlobal();

    while (1) { }
}
@endcode

@section sent_api API Quick Reference

@subsection sent_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function                    | Description                                              |
|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_DRV_Init()             | Initialize SENT instance with user configuration.        |
| SENT_DRV_Deinit()           | De-initialize SENT instance and reset registers.         |
| SENT_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() | Populate config struct with TLE4998 sensor defaults.     |

@subsection sent_api_fast Fast Message Operations
| Function                       | Description                                           |
|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_DRV_GetFastRxStatus()     | Check if a new Fast message is available.             |
| SENT_DRV_GetFastMsg()          | Read last received Fast message (clears Rx flag).     |
| SENT_DRV_GetFastMsgFromRaw()   | Convert a raw Fast message to structured format.      |
| SENT_DRV_SetFastMsgDmaBuffer() | Set/change DMA target buffer for Fast messages.       |

@subsection sent_api_slow Slow Message Operations
| Function                       | Description                                           |
|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_DRV_GetSlowRxStatus()     | Check if a new Slow message is available.             |
| SENT_DRV_GetSlowMsg()          | Read last received Slow message (clears Rx flag).     |
| SENT_DRV_GetSlowMsgFromRaw()   | Convert a raw Slow message to structured format.      |
| SENT_DRV_SetSlowMsgDmaBuffer() | Set/change DMA target buffer for Slow messages.       |

@subsection sent_api_callback Callback & Notification
| Function                         | Description                                         |
|----------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_DRV_SetRxCallbackFunction() | Set/change Rx callback and notification mode.       |

@subsection sent_api_diag Diagnostics & Events
| Function                | Description                                              |
|-------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_DRV_GetEvents()    | Read and clear active diagnostic event flags.            |

@subsection sent_api_spc SPC Control (Feature-gated)
| Function               | Description                                               |
|------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| SENT_DRV_SwTrigger()   | Generate software trigger for SPC pulse.                  |

@section sent_notes Important Notes

@warning The driver configures interrupt states, but the **interrupt priority
must be set by the application** before calling SENT_DRV_Init().

@warning The driver uses the **interrupt manager** and **DMA peripheral** as
shared resources. These must be configured and initialized before the SENT
driver.

@warning On MPC574xP devices, SENT module has **errata e7204**: "Number of
Expected Edges Error status flag spuriously set when operating with Option 1
of the Successive Calibration Check method." Workarounds:
- Enable the sensor before the peripheral driver (first message will not be received).
- Ignore the NUM_EDGES_ERR at startup.

@note The SENT peripheral clock must be enabled via the clock_manager
**before** calling SENT_DRV_Init(). The clock frequency must be at least
1 MHz.

@note Multiple SENT peripheral instances can be configured independently.
Each instance requires its own sent_state_t structure.

@note When using DMA mode, the DMA driver must be initialized and channels
allocated before calling SENT_DRV_Init().

@section sent_integration Integration Guide

@subsection sent_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source files must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/sent/sent_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/sent/sent_hw_access.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/sent/sent_irq.c
@endverbatim

@subsection sent_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directories to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/sent/
@endverbatim

@subsection sent_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
| Symbol                      | Description                                         |
|-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_SENT_HAS_INPUT_FILTER | Enables hardware glitch filter support.            |
| FEATURE_SENT_HAS_RECV_POLARITY| Enables receive polarity selection.                |
| FEATURE_SENT_HAS_SPC        | Enables SPC pulse generation support.               |
| FEATURE_SENT_DMA_HAS_FIFO   | Enables FIFO mode for Fast DMA transfers.           |
| ERRATA_E7425                | Enables workaround for errata E7425.                |

@subsection sent_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager — Required for enabling the SENT peripheral clock.
- DMA driver — Required when using DMA mode for message reception.
- Interrupt manager — Required for interrupt-driven and DMA modes.

*/
